# Paths excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# Two rules here are load-bearing for cache correctness, not tidiness:
#
#   1. `.docker-cache/` must be excluded. docker-compose.yml writes BuildKit
#      layer caches there; leaving it in the context would copy the cache into
#      the image and change the `COPY . .` hash on every build, invalidating
#      every layer after it.
#   2. The workspace exclusions use `**/`. A bare `out` or `dist` matches only
#      the repo root, so `apps/public-site/out` and `packages/*/dist` would still
#      ship to the daemon and bust the source layer whenever a previous build's
#      output changed.

# --- dependencies and build output ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
out
**/out
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# --- BuildKit layer cache (must stay excluded) ---
.docker-cache

# --- tests and reports (not needed to build or run the apps) ---
e2e
playwright.config.ts
playwright-report
test-results
**/*.spec.ts

# --- CI helper scripts (never imported by an app at build or runtime) ---
scripts/ci

# --- secrets: never bake these into an image ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- VCS, CI and agent config ---
.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.teamcity

# --- tool and agent state ---
.hermes
.kilo
.claude

# --- docs ---
docs/html
**/*.md

# --- misc ---
*.log